# Lucidchart packaging and import

## Source → package

1. Edit `path/to/diagram.lucid.json` (Standard Import document).
2. Validate JSON parses and has `version` + non-empty `pages`.
3. Package:

```bash
python3 plugins/lucidchart/skills/lucidchart-author/scripts/package_lucid.py \
  path/to/diagram.lucid.json path/to/diagram.lucid
```

The script writes a ZIP named `.lucid` whose only required member is
`document.json` (root `__layoutContract__` stripped).

## Create in Lucid (new document only)

Standard Import **cannot** patch an existing board. Always create a new doc:

```bash
curl 'https://api.lucid.co/v1/documents' \
  --request POST \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer $LUCID_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  --form 'file=@path/to/diagram.lucid;type=x-application/vnd.lucid.standardImport' \
  --form 'title=Diagram Title' \
  --form 'product=lucidchart'
```

Or import the `.lucid` file in the Lucid UI. Prefer MCP when a Lucid MCP is
connected and ready (`global-mcp-first`).

## Failure triage

| Symptom | Action |
|---|---|
| API 400 invalid payload | Diff JSON against SI schema; check shape `type`, required fields, unique ids |
| API 415 | Ensure form `type=x-application/vnd.lucid.standardImport` and `.lucid` zip |
| Lines look wrong after import | Elbow control points must be 90°; joints on buses only |
| “Repair in Lucid UI” ask | Edit `*.lucid.json`, re-package, re-import — do not claim in-place API edits |

For layout defects in the JSON, use `lucidchart-repair`. For new diagrams,
use `lucidchart-author`.
